      "dom_id": "question-45460",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Max initially had $$2$ in his piggy bank. Then, thanks to a generous relative, the amount of money in Max's piggy bank doubled at the end of every day. How much money will Max have in the piggy bank after $6$ days?",
      "worked_solution": "Initially, Max has $$2$ in the piggy bank, and this amount doubles every day.\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ day, Max has $2\\cdot 2$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ days, Max will have $2\\cdot (2)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ days, Max will have $2\\cdot (2)^{3}$ dollars.\n\n- $…$\n\n- After $6$ days, Max will have $2\\cdot (2)^{6}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the expression for its value after $6$ days, we get:\n\n$$\n2\\cdot (2)^{6}=2\\cdot 64=128\n$$\n\nThus, Max will have $$128$ after $6$ days.",
