      "dom_id": "question-45479",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The number of ants in a building triples every month. If there were $3\\,000$ ants initially, how many ants will there be after $3$ months?",
      "worked_solution": "Initially, there were $3,000$ ants, and this number triples every month.\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ month, there will be $3\\,000\\cdot 3$ ants.\n\n- After $2$ months, the will be $3\\,000\\cdot (3)^{2}$ ants.\n\n- After $3$ months, there will be $3\\,000\\cdot (3)^{3}$ ants.\n\nEvaluating the expression for the number of ants after $3$ months, we get:\n\n$$\n3,000\\cdot (3)^{3}=3,000\\cdot 27=81,000\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ months, there will be $81,000$ ants",
